t \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0edb1c73-87ee-58c2-a730-43e7f693d596" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330078} {:answer/id #uuid "26074d64-e780-5986-be16-fa82ceeb0164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330281} {:answer/id #uuid "3ec2d31d-3894-565f-9b91-3bc180c6d541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330506} {:answer/id #uuid "581c2751-ecf3-5021-a41f-a828e408e3cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330735} {:answer/id #uuid "59dbc6dd-87a6-5e93-99fe-8c88f23299aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{9}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ec2d31d-3894-565f-9b91-3bc180c6d541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330506} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef0aa3c5-1f7e-5feb-b2ae-0f439aa2181d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186332622}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea76ea1f-1600-5c9d-b198-b9fb197580ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-49548" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{9\\cdot (1+{x}^{2}/9)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}/9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=3\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{9+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b46bc9-97cb-5bce-918b-8b92646973b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247570} {:answer/id #uuid "1b1e75f2-49eb-5a5d-9cee-c6ed60930c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247668} {:answer/id #uuid "3de5bd43-5bd8-5d01-8064-06ac8fdb185f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247970} {:answer/id #uuid "c07e9314-0212-563d-818b-d17717a081be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}