{6}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=6\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{36+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{1+(x/6)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (6\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{x}{6}\\right)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc0eaaa6-3c74-5955-ab7a-40c09fa2a964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368718} {:answer/id #uuid "6b672eef-fdca-5016-828c-47d6af33c13e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368719} {:answer/id #uuid "ce69df23-6261-537f-bc31-f5d9599f5543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368720} {:answer/id #uuid "b7c8552a-dd1c-59c6-825b-7bdb5b09d5cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368721} {:answer/id #uuid "250a9a15-df5f-58ee-9c74-d26e624f24b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "250a9a15-df5f-58ee-9c74-d26e624f24b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368722} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b4164c5-58af-56ae-8f11-f8cd84fa0fda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368717}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c6decd4b-7a1d-5fb8-8bf2-963b2f6581d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73713" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{10}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $4{x}^{2}=(2x)^{2}.$\n\nSo. let's substitute $u=2x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{10}{1+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10\\int \\frac{1}{1+(2x)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =5\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b31a011-34d6-54fb-97d3-f5fd61f6b537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427995} {:answer/id #uuid "68c27e18-cd86-5136-97ff-930ab97daa47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427996} {:answer/id #uuid "74bba607-5459-5096-9775-251242509188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427997} {:answer/id #uuid "bbcb8ff0-bcc8-5c73-8990-398286767616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(6x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428001} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2fa96a-ca7c-53d2-b91f-002c52d75021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b31a011-34d6-54fb-97d3-f5fd61f6b537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427995} :answer-field/id #uuid "a430fc00-ecdb-5355-9c79-98aa358084c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186428004}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "276f25e8-0fe6-5cab-8eeb-f55147c6c339" :question/math-academy-id "q-114039" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{1}{1+6{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $6{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{6}x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{6}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{6}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+6{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+(\\sqrt{6}x)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{6}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Indefinite Integrals Using Substitution with Inverse Tangent"}]}
